hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18090","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shubah informed us from Sad ibn Ibrahim from Nasr ibn Abd al-Rahman from his grandfather Muadh ibn Afra al-Qurashi that he circumambulated the House with Muadh son of Afra after Asr or after dawn, then he did not pray, then I asked him, then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prayer after two prayers: after the morning until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."
"18091","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Ibrahim informed me, he said: I heard Nasr ibn Abd al-Rahman from his grandfather Muadh son of Afra that he circumambulated with Muadh son of Afra, then he did not pray after Asr or after dawn, then he said: What prevents you from praying. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding, or saying: No prayer after dawn until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."
